<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William the Silent</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1533–1584</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as William I, Prince of Orange, William of Orange</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William the Silent, Prince of Orange from 1544, was born at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dillenburg">Dillenburg</a> into the house of Nassau. He led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-revolt">Dutch Revolt</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-spain">Philip II of Spain</a> from 1568, and the northern provinces renounced Philip in 1581. He was assassinated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delft">Delft</a> in 1584 and is honoured as the father of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> nation and founder of the house of Orange-Nassau.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-the-silent.jpg" alt="William the Silent" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adriaen Thomasz. Key · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:William_I,_Prince_of_Orange_by_Adriaen_Thomasz._Key_Rijksmuseum_Amsterdam_SK-A-3148.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
